==Battleground==
*20 [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
*3 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 41.33~46.67 seconds<sup>1,240f~1,400f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[J.K. Bun Bun]] spawns as the boss.
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 10~16.67 seconds<sup>300f~500f</sup>.
**5 [[Shy Boy]]s spawn, delay 15.33~18.67 seconds<sup>460f~560f</sup>.
**2 [[Hackey]]s spawn, delay 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
**1 [[Professor A.]] spawns.

==Strategy==
Use [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshields]] along with units that can either deal damage or act as [[:Category:Crowd-Controller-class Cats|crowd-controllers]], such as [[Adult Cat (Rare Cat)|Prisoner Cat]], [[Apple Cat (Super Rare Cat)|iCat]], and even [[Red Riding Mina (Special Cat)|Crimson Mina]]. [[Sushi Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Roe Cat]] is a great choice for its resistance to [[:Category:Red Enemies|Red]] and extremely high health, especially at level 40 and above.

Do not bring [[Nerd Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Cyberpunk Cat]] or [[Asiluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Asilan Pasalan]] as they will get reduced to atoms by the Hackeys. [[Tecoluga (Uber Rare Cat)|Lufalan Pasalan]] can shine, outranging every enemy in the stage while also being able to enter the Hackeys' blind spots. [[Sharpshooter Saki (Uber Rare Cat)|Sharpshooter Saki]] is an excellent choice and can take out the Professor As early.

